'''

HELP_CHECK = '''\
Read every added file and compare its checksum with the one in the
repository. This is the full check and takes as long as reading all
the data.

First the names and the sizes are compared, as 'vrfdir status' does.
If an added file is deleted, its size has changed or it is not a
regular file anymore, the checksums are not checked at all. Run
'vrfdir status' to see those files. The files which are not added are
ignored.

The checksum of manifest.json itself is verified first. If it does
not match, nothing is checked: the damage is in manifest.json and
the checksums of the files cannot be trusted.

A file with a wrong checksum is printed on its own line (a name with
a newline is escaped, see 'vrfdir --help'):

  M  the content of the file has changed

A file which cannot be read is an error and the rest of the files are
still checked. If a directory cannot be read, the checksums are not
checked at all.

exit codes:
  0    the checksums of all the files match
  1    differences: a file is deleted, its size has changed or it is
       not a regular file anymore, the checksums were not checked
  2    corruption: the checksum of a file does not match
  3    error: a file could not be read and no checksum was wrong,
       a directory could not be read, or the repository is missing
       or cannot be read
  64   wrong command line
  130  interrupted
'''

