exit codes:
  0    the files were printed
  3    error, for example some files still have an MD5 checksum, or
       the repository is missing or cannot be read
  64   wrong command line
  130  interrupted
'''

HELP_UPGRADE = '''\
Upgrade a repository written by an older vrfdir to the latest format.
Nothing is done if the repository is already up to date.

Files which cannot be upgraded, for example because they were
changed or deleted, are listed. The rest of the files are still
upgraded. Run 'vrfdir status' or 'vrfdir check' to see what is wrong
with them. A name with a newline is escaped, see 'vrfdir --help'. If
both a changed file and an error are found, the exit code is the one
of the changed file.

exit codes:
  0    the repository is up to date
  1    differences: a file is deleted or its size has changed, it was
       not upgraded
  2    corruption: the content of a file has changed, it was not
       upgraded
  3    error: a file or a directory could not be read, or the
       repository is missing or cannot be read
  64   wrong command line
  130  interrupted, what was upgraded so far is saved
'''

HELP_INFO = '''\
Show information about the repository:

  Format       the version of the format of .vrfdir/manifest.json
  Manifest     the checksum of the content of manifest.json, which
               vrfdir verifies every time it reads the repository. A
               repository of an older format has none until
               'vrfdir upgrade' or 'vrfdir add' saves it
  Files        the number of the added files
  Total size   the total size of the added files
  Checksums    how many files have a SHA-256 and how many an MD5
               checksum, the latter are replaced by 'vrfdir upgrade'
